  "description": "XUHPIC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H84 Ce3 O12. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce10 (Ce) has 6 O neighbors; Ce11 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce12 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.614-3.751 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.18-104.45°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce(OiPr)4]3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OiPr (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
